Kix Retail — Sales Performance Analysis Dashboard

An end-to-end sales analytics project built in Excel using Power Query, Power Pivot (Data Model), and DAX, with interactive dashboards for revenue, target, and refund performance across stores, products, and time.

Problem Statement

Kix Retail operates across multiple stores and product categories but had no consolidated way to see whether stores were hitting their monthly revenue targets, which products or salespeople were driving performance, and where refunds were eating into profit. Sales, target, product, customer, and roster data lived in separate flat tables with no relationships between them, making it difficult to answer basic questions like:

Are we tracking ahead of or behind target, overall and by store/month?
Which stores are underperforming against their targets, and by how much?
How much of revenue comes from weekday vs. weekend trading?
What is the refund rate, and how much margin does it cost?
Which products, salespeople, and months contribute most to revenue?

This project builds a single connected data model from the raw tables and a set of dashboards to answer these questions on demand, instead of manually recompiling numbers every month.

Data Model

The workbook uses Power Pivot to build a star-schema data model, connecting one central fact table to several supporting dimension tables via Power Query:

Table	Role	Purpose
fact_table	Fact	Transaction-level sales records (revenue, quantity, refunds, etc.)
Date	Dimension	Calendar table (day, month name, weekday/weekend flag) for time intelligence
Dim_customers	Dimension	Customer attributes
products_table	Dimension	Product / category attributes
sales_persons_table	Dimension	Store and salesperson attributes
monthly_store_targets	Dimension/Reference	Monthly revenue target per store
Calculations	Measures table	Holds the DAX measures used across all dashboards

Relationships were built between the fact table and each dimension (typically one-to-many) so that a single slicer selection (store, month, category, weekday/weekend) filters every visual consistently — the core benefit of moving from flat tables to a proper data model.

Key DAX measures created: Total Revenue, Total Target, COGS, Profit Margin, Profit Margin %, Total Refund, Refund Rate, Transactions, Products, Total Qty Sold, Total Qty Returned.

Dashboards
Kix Business Dashboard — overall KPI dashboard
Sales Analysis Dashboard — store/product/time drill-down with slicers
Analysis 1 / Analysis 2 — supporting PivotTables (revenue vs. target, store performance, weekday/weekend split, monthly trend)
Waffle Chart — weekday vs. weekend revenue mix, visualized as a 10x10 waffle grid
