Key Takeaways
The business is ahead of target overall (+3.65%), but that headline number masks store-level trouble: 4 of 10 stores are behind target, with Novak PLC and Berg-Trujillo the biggest gaps.
Berg-Trujillo underperforms consistently, not seasonally — it missed target in 9 of 12 months, pointing to a store-specific issue worth investigating (staffing, footfall, local competition).
Refund rate (8.05%) is material against a 42.18% margin — reducing refunds even modestly would have a direct, outsized effect on profit.
Weekday trading dominates revenue (71.5%), which should inform staffing and promotional timing.
Revenue is stable across months with no extreme seasonality, aside from a dip in February.
